# code-review-graph CLI

Use `uvx code-review-graph` for graph lifecycle and change-analysis workflows.

## Prerequisites

```bash
uvx code-review-graph --help
```

Optional (for local install instead of `uvx`):

```bash
pipx install code-review-graph
code-review-graph --help
```

## Core Commands

### Build / Update Graph

```bash
# Full rebuild
uvx code-review-graph build --repo /abs/path/to/repo

# Incremental update (default base: HEAD~1)
uvx code-review-graph update --repo /abs/path/to/repo --base HEAD~1

# Faster update without flow/community work
uvx code-review-graph update --repo /abs/path/to/repo --skip-flows
```

### Change Analysis

```bash
# Full change analysis
uvx code-review-graph detect-changes --repo /abs/path/to/repo --base HEAD~1

# Brief summary output
uvx code-review-graph detect-changes --repo /abs/path/to/repo --brief
```

### Status / Postprocess

```bash
# Graph stats and health
uvx code-review-graph status --repo /abs/path/to/repo

# Recompute postprocess artifacts on existing graph
uvx code-review-graph postprocess --repo /abs/path/to/repo

# Targeted postprocess run
uvx code-review-graph postprocess --repo /abs/path/to/repo --no-fts
```

### Visualization / Wiki

```bash
# Generate interactive HTML graph
uvx code-review-graph visualize --repo /abs/path/to/repo --format html

# Serve visualization locally (localhost:8765)
uvx code-review-graph visualize --repo /abs/path/to/repo --serve

# Generate architecture/community wiki pages
uvx code-review-graph wiki --repo /abs/path/to/repo
```

### Multi-Repo Registry

```bash
# Register repo with optional alias
uvx code-review-graph register /abs/path/to/repo --alias myrepo

# List registered repos
uvx code-review-graph repos

# Remove by alias or path
uvx code-review-graph unregister myrepo
```

### Continuous / Evaluation

```bash
# Watch repo and auto-update graph
uvx code-review-graph watch --repo /abs/path/to/repo

# Run all benchmark suites
uvx code-review-graph eval --all

# Run selected benchmarks
uvx code-review-graph eval --benchmark token_efficiency,impact_accuracy
```

## MCP Tool Coverage Mapping

The CLI currently exposes these top-level workflows directly:
- `build`, `update`, `postprocess`, `status`, `detect-changes`, `visualize`, `wiki`, `watch`, `register`, `unregister`, `repos`, `eval`, `serve`

Some MCP tools do not currently have a one-command CLI equivalent (for example `query_graph_tool`, `get_review_context_tool`, `get_impact_radius_tool`, `refactor_tool`, `apply_refactor_tool`, `semantic_search_nodes_tool`).

Use the MCP surface when you need those fine-grained graph queries/refactors.

## Most Common Recipes

```bash
# 1) First-time setup for a repo
uvx code-review-graph build --repo /abs/path/to/repo
uvx code-review-graph status --repo /abs/path/to/repo

# 2) Review the latest diff quickly
uvx code-review-graph update --repo /abs/path/to/repo --base HEAD~1
uvx code-review-graph detect-changes --repo /abs/path/to/repo --base HEAD~1 --brief

# 3) Generate docs artifacts for architecture review
uvx code-review-graph wiki --repo /abs/path/to/repo
uvx code-review-graph visualize --repo /abs/path/to/repo --format html
```

## Troubleshooting

- `No graph found` or empty status:
  - Run `uvx code-review-graph build --repo /abs/path/to/repo` first.
- `fatal: bad revision 'HEAD~1'`:
  - Use a valid base: `--base HEAD` or a concrete commit SHA.
- Wrong repository analyzed:
  - Always pass `--repo /abs/path/to/repo` to avoid cwd ambiguity.
